WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:01.269
Speaker 1: you know, the biggest beneficiary
of the last 24 hours, 48 hours, 72 hours of

00:00:01.269 --> 00:00:02.269
coverage of the Derek Chauvin case and other
things.

00:00:02.269 --> 00:00:03.269
The biggest beneficiary has been Matt Gates,
who has been able to get a respite from the

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:04.269
focus on him, but he is still in full damage
control mode.

00:00:04.269 --> 00:00:05.269
We're going to talk about that after the break.

00:00:05.269 --> 00:00:06.269
And we are also hearing about a Republican
that supposedly is moving in the direction

00:00:06.269 --> 00:00:07.269
of running for president in twenty, twenty
four.

00:00:07.269 --> 00:00:08.269
I will tell you who it is and the implications
right after this short break.

00:00:08.269 --> 00:00:09.269
As I mentioned before the break, one of the
biggest beneficiaries of the last 48 to 72

00:00:09.269 --> 00:00:10.610
hours of the news cycle being on the Derek
Chauvin case has been Republican Congressman

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:15.750
Matt Gates, who is in full, full damage control
mode.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:19.200
He should be in resignation mode, not damage
control mode.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.810
And I believe that the attention is going
to get back to Matt Gates.

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:29.810
There's a very interesting Daily Beast article
which points out that quotes his latest campaign

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:35.239
finance report, reflects a public relations
scramble that began even before he acknowledged

00:00:35.239 --> 00:00:38.210
being the focus of a federal investigation.

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:43.110
We now are learning that Matt Gates knew much
earlier that he was the focus of this investigation

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:47.920
and that he was already working on his public
relations campaign.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:52.560
The filing, which covers the three months
between January and March, writes The Daily

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:58.170
Beast, shows that Gates has incurred unprecedented
fundraising expenses during a typically quiet

00:00:58.170 --> 00:00:59.170
period.

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:04.420
In that time, Gates dropped six figures on
a direct mail blitz, shelling out more for

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:07.030
fundraising services than he did in all of
2012.

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:09.580
We now understand the cycle.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:14.229
One of my criticisms of the status quo of
the House of Representatives and two year

00:01:14.229 --> 00:01:20.819
terms is that with two year terms, you basically
get elected, you get six months and then you

00:01:20.819 --> 00:01:22.670
start campaigning again.

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:27.439
Matt Gates is doing the fundraising during
that six month period where you are typically

00:01:27.439 --> 00:01:28.509
not campaigning.

00:01:28.509 --> 00:01:31.359
It's basically a year and a half of campaigning,
not to.

00:01:31.359 --> 00:01:36.320
Matt Gates is starting right away, and it
tells us quite a bit about the panic that

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:39.170
he is likely feeling as a result of these
investigations.

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:43.929
The article goes on to say, Gates also paid
five thousand dollars in strategic consulting

00:01:43.929 --> 00:01:49.990
fees to notorious political operative Roger
Stone, and he gave money to a number of Republican

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:53.359
Florida state lawmakers that he has never
supported before.

00:01:53.359 --> 00:01:54.829
Would it appears he's trying to do there.

00:01:54.829 --> 00:01:58.069
And again, we're left to read into the actions
of a madman.

00:01:58.069 --> 00:02:02.420
It seems he's trying to curry favor with some
of these fellow Florida Republicans so that

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:07.159
they will not abandon him and hopefully will
speak out in his support if and when it gets

00:02:07.159 --> 00:02:10.000
really, really ugly for him, which could be
any time.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:15.320
The Daily Beast writes that the report also
indicates Gates may be increasingly isolated.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:19.480
He's received no contributions from his Republican
colleagues.

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:23.980
More than anything, the filing reflects a
concerted effort to bolster support ahead

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:26.260
of the creeping shadow of the investigation.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:29.890
Gates has spent roughly one hundred and seventy
K on direct mail this year.

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:33.490
One hundred and sixty thousand of it all on
one day, March 31st.

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:39.930
I think that's the day after I know I was
on or I was on our break that day.

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:44.220
That must be the day after the bizarre interview
with Tucker Carlson.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:48.510
The previous day, The New York Times broke
the news that the Justice Department was looking

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:53.490
into whether he had sex with a 17 year old
and paid for her travel, which possibly violates

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:56.320
federal sex trafficking laws.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:03:01.430
Gates has also invested in fundraising, paying
Nevada based Redrock Strategies nearly one

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:05.340
hundred and sixty K for fundraising consulting.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:12.300
That's more than he spent on fundraising services
in 2019 and 2020 combined.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.370
That is stunning.

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:19.270
Last week, Politico reported Gates spent six
figures on TV ads punching back against the

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:25.770
accusations, 30 second spot slated to run
in his home district in the Florida Panhandle

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:33.590
and on national cable networks, asking supporters
to, quote, fight back against a, quote, multi

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:38.310
week fake news cycle targeting CNN.

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:43.580
There is one expense in particular, raising
eyebrows, a five thousand dollar strategic

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:47.660
political consulting fee to Drake Ventures.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:50.770
That's the company belonging to Roger Stone.

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:56.880
Friday, the Department of Justice sued Stone
and his wife, saying they owed millions of

00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:04.120
dollars in unpaid taxes and are using that
very same Drak ventures to shelter more than

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:05.690
one million dollars.

00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:06.690
Isn't that unbelievable?

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:12.580
Look at look at how the tentacles of gates
are spreading into so many different things.

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:16.400
So there's the investigation into Gates, which
we already talked about.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:22.099
And then now in light of that, it's sort of
weird that Gates was the lone no vote on some

00:04:22.099 --> 00:04:24.700
sex trafficking bill a couple of years ago
or whatever.

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:25.700
Okay, that's weird.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:28.050
And we're starting to see that in a new light.

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:34.840
Then we learn about Gates's alleged involvement
in a shill candidate scheme in a different

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:37.060
district in the state of Florida.

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:41.620
We had a report on that, I believe it was
earlier mid last week.

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:47.600
Now we find out that Gates paid a consulting
fee to Roger Stone's company.

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:56.599
And it is the very same company that now allegedly
is a way for Roger Stone and his wife to shelter

00:04:56.599 --> 00:05:00.259
more than a million dollars and avoid paying.

00:05:00.259 --> 00:05:01.259
Taxes.

00:05:01.259 --> 00:05:06.189
It's so tied in with all of this stuff and
in a sense, I don't feel bad for him, but

00:05:06.189 --> 00:05:10.770
Gates may end up being another sort of victim
of the Trump grift.

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:16.009
The way that the Trump grift works is Trump
loves you, loves you, loves you for as long

00:05:16.009 --> 00:05:20.710
as you are saying good things about him and
for as long as you are useful to him and Trump

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:22.719
will introduce you to all sorts of different
people.

00:05:22.719 --> 00:05:27.729
Who knows how Matt Gates ended up sort of
entangled with Roger Stone in the first place?

00:05:27.729 --> 00:05:30.600
My instinct is that it has something to do
with Donald Trump.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:35.360
As soon as you are no longer useful to Trump
or as soon as you are potentially a problem

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:39.850
due to your own issues that you were having
from a public relations standpoint, Trump

00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:41.520
is gone.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:46.509
And indeed, the reports are that Matt Gates
has been trying to meet with Trump.

00:05:46.509 --> 00:05:50.889
Matt Gates has been claiming that he has Donald
Trump support, although it's not completely

00:05:50.889 --> 00:05:52.980
clear that that's the case.

00:05:52.980 --> 00:05:55.789
And it is another in at least partially.

00:05:55.789 --> 00:05:57.979
I'm not saying Gates did the stuff.

00:05:57.979 --> 00:06:02.159
If Gates did the stuff he's accused of doing,
he didn't do it because of Donald Trump.

00:06:02.159 --> 00:06:06.889
But he is another one of these guys who got
sort of lulled into Trump's circle as a brownnosing

00:06:06.889 --> 00:06:11.349
sycophant and then dropped like a bad habit
as soon as he was no longer useful.

00:06:11.349 --> 00:06:15.840
One other piece of this very extensive Daily
Beast article about what's going on with Matt

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:20.180
Gates quote, The report also suggests Gates
has few friends in Washington.

00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:24.669
While Gates swore off donations from corporate
PACs, he kept the door open to donations from

00:06:24.669 --> 00:06:25.669
candidate committees.

00:06:25.669 --> 00:06:30.139
But he has so far reported no financial support
in twenty twenty one from friends in Congress

00:06:30.139 --> 00:06:35.259
like Jim Jordan and Steve Scalise, both of
whom donated back in 2020.

00:06:35.259 --> 00:06:41.039
While Gates made the same day four thousand
dollar donations to Mike Lee and Rand Paul.

00:06:41.039 --> 00:06:44.270
Gates did not give money to any House colleagues.

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:49.869
He did send out a thousand, a few five one
thousand dollar donations to five Republican

00:06:49.869 --> 00:06:54.400
Florida senators and had not donated to their
campaigns previously.

00:06:54.400 --> 00:07:02.169
So I would expect that the media attention
will go back to Matt Gates at some point relatively

00:07:02.169 --> 00:07:04.300
soon, at some point relatively soon.

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:07.919
I would imagine we will know whether there
will be charges filed as a result of what

00:07:07.919 --> 00:07:11.599
appear to be multiple investigations into
Matt Gates.

00:07:11.599 --> 00:07:16.639
But certainly Gates must be thrilled that
for the last two to three days, the focus

00:07:16.639 --> 00:07:18.789
has been not on him, but rather on Derek.

00:07:18.789 --> 00:07:19.679
Shervin, we'll get back to him, no question
about it.

